4.	Dispute Resolution. 

4.1	PLEASE READ THIS SECTION CAREFULLY – IT SIGNIFICANTLY AFFECTS YOUR LEGAL RIGHTS, INCLUDING YOUR RIGHT TO FILE A LAWSUIT IN COURT AND TO HAVE A JURY HEAR YOUR CLAIMS. IT CONTAINS PROCEDURES FOR MANDATORY BINDING ARBITRATION AND A CLASS ACTION WAIVER.

If you have an issue that cannot be resolved quickly and amicably by contacting our customer support at https://darkanddarker.com/support/contact or support@ironmace.com this Dispute Resolution section explains how you and we agree to resolve any Dispute (defined below), including (where applicable) by binding, individual arbitration.

a.	General Arbitration Details. Arbitration is an alternative dispute-resolution process that allows you and us to try to resolve Disputes (defined below) without the formality or expense of litigating in court. Arbitration is often faster and less expensive than formal litigation. Disputes that are subject to arbitration are submitted to a neutral arbitrator, who has the power to award the same damages and relief that a court can, instead of being presented in court to a judge or jury. If you wish to opt-out of this binding individual arbitration requirement, you must comply with the opt-out process set forth in the “Opt-Out Right” paragraph below. This binding individual arbitration requirement will not apply to the extent prohibited by the laws of your country of residence.

b.	Informal Negotiation Process. In an effort to help us get to a resolution faster and reduce the costs for both parties, you and we agree to first attempt to informally negotiate any Dispute for at least 30 days (except as set out in the “Exclusions from Arbitration” section below). Those informal negotiations will start on the day you or we receive a written Notice of a Dispute as set out below. For the avoidance of doubt, we may decide to suspend or terminate this Addendum, the Game Terms or any other applicable terms, and/or your access to any part of Dark and Darker if we determine you have violated any term of this Addendum, the Game Terms or any other applicable terms. Our decisions are not subject to any informal negotiation process.

If you have a Dispute with us, you will send written notice to Ironmace Co. Ltd. at 8F, 225-18, Pangyoyeok-ro Bundang-gu, Seongnam-si, Gyeonggi-do, Republic of Korea or via email at support@ironmace.com, in order to give us the opportunity to resolve the Dispute through informal negotiation (“Notice of Dispute”). Include your name, account name, or registered email address you use to access Dark and Darker, your address, how to contact you, what the problem is, and what you want us to do about it. If we have a Dispute with you, we will send our Notice of Dispute to your registered email address and any billing address you have provided us.  If the Dispute isn’t resolved through informal negotiation, you or we may start an arbitration as set forth in this Addendum.

c.	Binding Individual Arbitration. THE ARBITRATION PROCEEDINGS IN THIS SECTION WILL BE CONDUCTED ON AN INDIVIDUAL BASIS ONLY.

Arbitration Rules. The arbitration will be administered by the American Arbitration Association (“AAA”) in accordance with the Commercial Arbitration Rules and the Supplementary Procedures for Consumer Related Disputes (the “AAA Rules”) then in effect, except as modified by this Dispute Resolution Section. (The AAA Rules are available at https://www.adr.org/mediation or by calling the AAA at 1–800–778–7879.) The Federal Arbitration Act will govern the interpretation and enforcement of this Dispute Resolution Section.

Arbitration Process. A party who desires to initiate arbitration must provide the other party with a written Demand for Arbitration as specified in the AAA Rules (The AAA provides a form Demand for Arbitration). The arbitrator will be either a retired judge or an attorney licensed to practice law and will be selected by the parties from the AAA’s roster of arbitrators. If the parties are unable to agree upon an arbitrator within seven (7) days of delivery of the Demand for Arbitration, then the AAA will appoint the arbitrator in accordance with the AAA Rules.

Arbitration Location and Procedure. Unless you and we otherwise agree, the arbitration will be conducted in the state where you reside, with the option for you to participate telephonically to the extent the AAA Rules allow. If your claim does not exceed $10,000, then the arbitration will be conducted solely on the basis of the documents that you and we submit to the arbitrator, unless you request a hearing, or the arbitrator determines that a hearing is necessary. If your claim exceeds $10,000, your right to a hearing will be determined by the AAA Rules. Subject to the AAA Rules, the arbitrator will have the discretion to direct a reasonable exchange of information by the parties, consistent with the expedited nature of the arbitration. 

Arbitrator’s Decision. The arbitrator will render an award within the time frame specified in the AAA Rules. The arbitrator’s decision will include the essential findings and conclusions which the arbitrator based its award on. Judgment on the arbitration award may be entered in any court having jurisdiction over the arbitration award. The arbitrator’s award of damages must be consistent with the terms of the “Limitation of Liability” Section of this Addendum as to the types and amounts of damages for which a party may be held liable. The arbitrator may award declaratory or injunctive relief only in favor of the claimant and only to the extent necessary to provide relief warranted by the claimant’s individual claim. If you prevail in arbitration, you will be entitled to an award of attorneys’ fees and expenses, to the extent provided under applicable law. We will not seek, and hereby waives all rights it may have under applicable law to recover, attorneys’ fees and expenses if we prevail in arbitration, unless such arbitration is found by the arbitrator to be frivolous under the standards of the Federal Rules of Civil Procedure 11(b) and in that case, we shall be entitled to recover attorneys’ fees in addition to any damages awarded to it.

Fees. If the arbitrator finds that your payment of the administrative and arbitrator fees (excluding any attorney’s fees) under this subsection is a burden on you, we agree to pay those fees for you (but not any attorney’s fees). 

Changes. By rejecting any changes to this Addendum, you agree that you will arbitrate any Dispute between you and we in accordance with the provisions of this Section as of the date you first accepted these Terms (or accepted any subsequent changes to these Terms).

Your Choices. If you do not want to settle Disputes by arbitration as described above, you will notify us by sending us written notice (including by email to support@ironmace.com telling us that you do not want to use arbitration, within thirty (30) days of the date on which you agreed to this Addendum (such notice, an “Arbitration Opt-out Notice”). If you do not provide us with an Arbitration Opt-out Notice within the thirty (30) day period, you will be deemed to have knowingly and intentionally waived your right to litigate any dispute except for a Small Claims Action and an IP Protection Action as stated above.

d.	No Class Actions. TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY APPLICABLE LAW, YOU AND WE AGREE TO BRING DISPUTES UNDER THIS AGREEMENT ON AN INDIVIDUAL BASIS ONLY. The arbitrator may not combine or consolidate individual proceedings unless all parties to this Agreement and all other actions or arbitrations expressly consents to such consolidation. Neither you nor we may arbitrate any dispute in a representative capacity, including, without limitation, as a representative member of a class, collective or class-wide arbitration, or in private attorney general actions. The arbitrator may award any relief permitted by applicable law with respect to your individual claim, but to the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, may not award relief against us respecting any person other than you.  

e.	Severability. If any clause within this Binding Individual Arbitration agreement is found to be invalid, unenforceable, or illegal, that clause will be severed and the remainder of this arbitration agreement will be given full force and effect. The only exception to this is the “No Class Actions” paragraph. If the “No Class Actions” paragraph is found to be invalid, illegal or unenforceable in its entirety, this entire arbitration agreement will be void and unenforceable, and the Dispute will proceed in court. Under no circumstances shall arbitration be conducted on a class basis without our express consent. If, for any reason, a claim proceeds in court rather than in arbitration, the dispute shall be exclusively brought in the applicable court in the Republic of Korea. 

f.	Your 30-Day Opt-Out Right. YOU HAVE THE RIGHT TO OPT OUT OF THIS BINDING INDIVIDUAL ARBITRATION REQUIREMENT AND CLASS ACTION WAIVER. IF YOU DO NOT WISH TO BE BOUND BY THE BINDING INDIVIDUAL ARBITRATION AND CLASS ACTION WAIVER IN THIS AGREEMENT, YOU MUST NOTIFY US IN WRITING OF YOUR INTENT TO DO SO WITHIN 30 DAYS OF THE DATE THAT YOU FIRST ACCEPT THIS AGREEMENT UNLESS A LONGER PERIOD IS REQUIRED BY APPLICABLE LAW. Your written notification must be  sent to Ironmace Co. Ltd. at 8F, 225-18, Pangyoyeok-ro Bundang-gu, Seongnam-si, Gyeonggi-do, Republic of Korea or via email at support@ironmace.com. Your notice must include (1) your full name; (2) your mailing address; (3) your user account name, if you have one; and (4) a clear statement that you do not wish to resolve disputes with us through arbitration. You are responsible for ensuring our receipt of your opt-out notice, and you therefore may wish to send a notice by means that provide a written receipt of delivery.

5.	Limitation of Liability. TO THE FULLEST EXTENT PERMITTED BY APPLICABLE LAW, IN NO EVENT SHALL WE BE LIABLE TO YOU FOR ANY  INDIRECT, SPECIAL, INCIDENTAL, EXEMPLARY, CONSEQUENTIAL OR PUNITIVE LOSSES OR DAMAGES, OR DAMAGES FOR SYSTEM FAILURE OR MALFUNCTION OR LOSS OF PROFITS, DATA, USE, BUSINESS OR GOOD-WILL, ARISING OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH DARK AND DARKER OR THIS ADDENDUM, WHETHER ARISING IN CONTRACT, TORT, STRICT LIABILITY, STATUTE OR ANY OTHER LEGAL OR EQUITABLE THEORY. 

In the event you have any basis for recovering damages arising from Dark and Darker or a breach of applicable terms, you agree that your exclusive remedy is to recover from us direct damages and the maximum liability is limited up to an amount equal to $500 USD. 

6.	Indemnification. To the fullest extent permitted by applicable law, you agree to defend, indemnify and hold us harmless from and against any and all claims, liabilities, damages, losses, costs and expenses (including, reasonable attorneys’ fees and costs) arising out of or in connection with: (i) your breach or alleged breach of this Addendum and/or the Game Terms; (ii) any information or content provided by you; and/or (iii) your acts or omissions. We reserve the right to assume, at our own expense, the exclusive defense and control of any matter subject to indemnification by you, and in such case you agree to cooperate with our defense of any claim. You are solely responsible for any third party costs you incur to use Dark and Darker, and you bear all risk of loss for accessing or downloading Dark and Darker.

7.	Export Laws. You must comply with all domestic and international export laws and regulations (which may be amended from time to time) that apply to Dark and Darker, which include restrictions on destinations, end users, and end use. You agree not to use, export, re-export, or download Dark and Darker into (or to a national or resident of) any country to which the U.S. has embargoed goods, or to anyone on the U.S. Treasury Department’s list of Specially Designated Nationals and Blocked Persons list and other sanctions lists administered by the Office of Foreign Assets Control (OFAC). You represent and warrant that you are not located in, under the control of, or a national or resident of a U.S. restricted or prohibited country or on any OFAC sanctions list.

8.	General. This Addendum, together with the Game Terms and any other applicable terms, is the entire agreement between you and us for your use of Dark and Darker and any other related content. We may assign our rights and obligations to you, in whole or in part, at any time without notice to you. You may not assign your rights or obligations or transfer any rights to use Dark and Darker. All parts of these terms apply to the fullest extent permitted by applicable law. If any provision of these terms are held to be unenforceable for any reason, such provision shall be reformed only to the extent necessary to make it enforceable and the remaining provisions of this Agreement shall not be affected. Paragraphs that, by their nature apply after this Addendum ends, will survive any termination or cancellation of this Addendum or applicable terms. We reserve the right to investigate and prosecute any suspected breaches of this Addendum, the Game Terms, or use of Dark and Darker. We may disclose any information as necessary to satisfy any law, regulation, legal process or governmental request. 

9.	Remedies. In the event that you breach this Addendum, Game Terms or applicable terms, you hereby agree that we would be irreparably damaged if such terms were not specifically enforced, and therefore you agree that we shall be entitled, without bond, other security, or proof of damages, to obtain equitable remedies with respect to breaches of such terms, in addition to such other remedies as we may otherwise have available to us under applicable laws. 

10.	Contact Us. If you are a U.S. resident and have questions about this Addendum or need assistance accessing this Addendum, please submit a ticket at https://darkanddarker.com/support/contact or contact us at support@ironmace.com. 


IRONMACE CODE OF CONDUCT 

1.	ABOUT THIS CODE OF CONDUCT

1.1	We, Ironmace Co. Ltd., take player safety and fairness in our games extremely seriously. This Code of Conduct sets out the rules which you must follow any time you play our games, access our content or interact with other users. They form part of the End User Licence Agreement of each of our games, including Dark and Darker. When you accept the End User Licence Agreement for the game, you agree to comply with this Code of Conduct as well. 

1.2	Breach of this Code of Conduct is considered a serious breach of our game End User Licence Agreement(s), which may result in your immediate suspension and/or permanent removal from the game and deletion of your account with us.

1.3	If you have any questions about this Code of Conduct, contact us by submitting a ticket at https://darkanddarker.com/support/contact (or email us at support@ironmace.com if you are unable to submit a ticket).

2.	CHEATING PROHIBITED

2.1	You agree not to do anything which is intended to hack, cheat, abuse, manipulate, change or otherwise obtain unauthorised access to any benefits or features in-game. Examples of prohibited cheating activities include (but are not limited to): 

(a)	using third party scripts, modifications, applications, programs or other software which enables or facilitates unauthorised changes or manipulation of game data; 

(b)	decompiling or reverse engineering the game code other than where the game Terms of Use expressly allow this;

(c)	abusing  or exploiting glitches, bugs or other errors in the game code; 

(d)	hardware or software methods to manipulate gameplay, including but not limited to aimbots, wallhacks, speed hacks, ESP (extra-sensory perception), radar hacks, and triggerbots;

(e)	using automation tools to farm in-game currency, items, or experience points;

(f)	using unauthorized crosshair overlays or custom reticles to gain an advantage

(g)	using recoil control scripts or macros to manage weapon behaviour unfairly;

(h)	employing sound modification tools to amplify or alter in-game audio cues for competitive advantage.

(i)	exploiting spawn points, map geometry, or unintended vantage points to gain an unfair advantage.

(j)	engaging in "ghosting" by using external information to influence in-game decisions unfairly.

(k)	using network manipulation techniques such as lag switching, DDoS attacks, or packet manipulation to disrupt gameplay.

(l)	colluding with other players to manipulate match outcomes, including win trading and boosting services.

(m)	sharing, distributing or selling cheats, hacks, or exploits to others;

(n)	using bots or other automated gameplay mechanisms; and

(o)	scraping, intercepting, mining or otherwise collecting information from our games without our consent.

3.	ANTI-CHEATING SOFTWARE AND DATA

3.1	To prevent cheating behaviours in-game, our games contain anti-cheating software known as “Ironshield”. This works by:

(a)	monitoring your hardware and processes;

(b)	analysing game binaries;

(c)	scanning and logging hardware identifiers and processes; 

(d)	taking snapshots of device memory and screenshots; and

(e)	logging other technical information as listed in section 3.3 below;

in each case only for the purpose of detecting and preventing cheating in our games.

3.2	We receive the technical information provided by Ironshield, and we only use this to check whether any individual user’s device is being used to cheat in our games in violation of the Terms of Use. Information about personal data we collect and how we use it is set out in our Privacy Policy available at www.darkanddarker.com/legal.

3.3	Where Ironshield detects any unauthorised activity, we will be notified of technical information about your computer, device, hardware, and software you use to access our services from you, these include:

(a)	game and account identifiers;

(b)	your IP address;

(c)	device identifiers;

(d)	information about the running operating system;

(e)	information about game-related and operating-system-related files and memory;

(f)	information about running processes, drivers and other executable code; and

(g)	in-game screenshots (of the game window only).

4.	GAME SECURITY  & DATA

4.1	You must not (and must not attempt to, or help anyone else to): 

(a)	circumvent, disable, or otherwise interfere with any security-related features;

(b)	use the game in any manner which goes against applicable laws or regulations;

(c)	sell or attempt to sell in-game currency, items or other resources outside the game environment (such as for real-world currency);

(d)	sell or otherwise transfer (or attempt to sell or otherwise transfer) your account to anyone else;  

(e)	upload, transmit, or distribute to or through our games or your account any computer viruses, worms, or any software intended to damage or alter a computer system or data;

(f)	include your personal data or other personal identifiers (such as your real name) in your username, on any in-game chat function, or on any public profile page; 

(g)	use our games or your account to harvest, collect, gather or assemble information or data regarding other users, including e-mail addresses, without their consent; or

(h)	attempt to gain unauthorised access to our games (or to other computer systems or networks connected to or used together with our games), whether through password mining or any other means.

5.	INTERACTIONS WITH OTHERS 

5.1	You must not (and must not attempt to, or help anyone else to): 

(a)	harass, threaten, bully, or engage in any abusive behaviour towards other players;

(b)	use offensive, hateful, or discriminatory language or content;

(c)	engage in account trading, selling, or sharing to gain unfair advantages;

(d)	impersonate any person, company, or representative of Ironmace;

(e)	be harassing, abusive, threatening, harmful, invasive of another’s privacy, vulgar, defamatory, false, intentionally misleading, pornographic, obscene, or offensive;

(f)	use the game or your account to send unsolicited or unauthorised advertising, promotional materials, junk mail, spam, chain letters, pyramid schemes, or any other form of duplicative or unsolicited messages, whether commercial or otherwise;

(g)	use the game or your account to harvest, collect, gather or assemble information or data regarding other users, including e-mail addresses, without their consent 

(h)	include your personal data or other personal identifiers (such as your real name) in your username, on any in-game chat function, or on any public profile page 

(i)	promote racism, bigotry, hatred, or physical harm of any kind against any group or individual or do anything which is otherwise offensive or objectionable; 

(j)	do anything which is harmful to minors in any way; or

(k)	participate in any activity that disrupts or negatively affects the gameplay experience of others; 

5.2	The following activities  may also lead to penalties and/or account suspension or removal: 

(a)	Team Killing: Intentionally killing teammates disrupts normal team gameplay. Repeated or deliberate team killing may result in penalties.

(b)	Unauthorized Teams: Teaming up with players or teams in ways not supported by the selected game mode is prohibited.

(c)	Stalking Other Players Across Matches: Repeatedly following or targeting specific players from match to match to disrupt their gameplay is prohibited and may result in penalties.

(d)	Playing with Cheaters: Participating in games with players who are known to be using cheats, hacks, or unauthorized software may result in penalties. If you knowingly benefit from or support cheaters, you may face the same disciplinary actions as the cheater.

6.	GAMBLING  

6.1	Gambling is not permitted in our games, whether it relates to real or in-game currency or items or any other prizes. You must not use our games for gambling activities, which includes:

(a)	in-game betting, unauthorised lotteries, or any form of wagering with real or virtual currencies;

(b)	organising, advertising, promoting, facilitating, exploiting or participating in any gambling activities;

(c)	using the in-game marketplace in connection with gambling;

(d)	streaming or otherwise producing or displaying content which relates to gambling in our games on any platform, 

and if you fail to comply with this, we will consider it a serious breach of these Game Terms and you may lose access to our games (including Dark and Darker) on a temporary or permanent basis.  

7.	CONSEQUENCES OF BREACHING THIS CODE OF CONDUCT

7.1	If we determine that you have breached this Code of Conduct, we have the right to:

(a)	apply restrictions to your account and/or playing experience  to maintain a fair gaming environment; 

(b)	exercise any of our rights under the applicable game End User Licence Agreement, including the right to suspend or terminate your access to the game without prior notice to you and without issuing any refund for content you have purchased from us; 

(c)	suspend or terminate any account you hold with us on a temporary or permanent basis; and/or

(d)	where your actions could constitute a breach of laws which apply to you, report you to appropriate law enforcement authorities.
